
== 1. heating and motional dephasing during the K-loop MS gate (Section 9.7 rows 1-2; exact engine, mesolve)
  K = 1: t_g = 50.0 us, base fidelity 0.9997; heating at 400 quanta/s: loss 9.649e-03 against ndot t_g/(2K) = 1.000e-02 (ratio 0.965); motional dephasing tau = t_g/5e-3: loss 3.297e-03 against alpha_K t_g/tau = 3.438e-03 (ratio 0.959)
  K = 2: t_g = 50.0 us, base fidelity 0.9998; heating at 400 quanta/s: loss 4.869e-03 against ndot t_g/(2K) = 5.000e-03 (ratio 0.974); motional dephasing tau = t_g/5e-3: loss 1.439e-03 against alpha_K t_g/tau = 1.484e-03 (ratio 0.969)
  the two-mode closure played with the rocking mode frozen over-rotates the gate and gives 0.84 and 0.80 of the closed forms (the M7 diagnostic)

== 2. intensity-noise channel c_op = sqrt(2k) H_int in the force model (Section 9.16 row 4.4-8)
  N = 2, K = 1: A/(Gamma_I t_g eta^2) = 1.0003 (the plan's derived form has 1/2), B/A = 0.7498 (derived 3(N-1)/(4K) = 0.7500; the printed (N-1)/4 term would give 0.5000)
  N = 2, K = 2: A/(Gamma_I t_g eta^2) = 1.0019 (the plan's derived form has 1/2), B/A = 0.3726 (derived 3(N-1)/(4K) = 0.3750; the printed (N-1)/4 term would give 0.5000)
  carrier-contrast definition: d<sigma_z>/dt / (k Omega^2 <sigma_z>) = 1.000000 under sqrt(2k)(Omega/2) sigma_x
  -> with Gamma_I the carrier-contrast rate the budget is Gamma_I t_g eta^2 (2 nbar + 1) + Gamma_I t_g eta^2 3(N-1)/(4K): twice the plan's derived A and B, the same ratio

